        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ਪਰਤਣਾ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਪਰਤਣਾ — paratṇā — \"to return; to come back\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਅਸੀਂ ਐਤਵਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਸ਼ਹਿਰ ਪਰਤਾਂਗੇ। asīṁ aitvār nū̃ shahir partāṅge. We will return to the city on Sunday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ਮੈਂ ਘਰ ਪਰਤਿਆ, maiṁ ghar partiā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਪਰਤਣਾ (paratṇā) is inherited from Sanskrit parivartatē, \"turns round\"; CDIAL lists Punjabi partaṇā under it only as \"to change the side of anything by turning it\"; the sense \"to return\" is the one it gives for Lahnda partaṇ (CDIAL 7872)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what comes next."
